---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /brand.html
title: "Monogram options — for review"
description: "ZT monogram options for Zachery Taylor's site, shown at favicon, navigation, and large sizes on light and dark backgrounds."
sheet: B-001
sheetTitle: "Brand — monogram options"
noSitemap: true
noindex: true
rounds:
  - title: "Round 2 — new directions"
    label: "B-002"
    options:
      - key: d
        name: "D · North arrow"
        note: "A surveyor's north arrow in a compass ring. The T is the arrow — half-filled north point, crossbar, shaft — and its crossbar doubles as the top of a bronze Z. Most ‘survey plat’ of the set."
      - key: e
        name: "E · Contour lines"
        note: "ZT as a ridge on a topographic map: the letters are the high ground and contour lines step out around them, merging where the letters meet, with a bronze index contour outermost."
      - key: f
        name: "F · Lettering stencil"
        note: "Bold stencil ZT cut from an ink lettering template (think Leroy guide), with stencil bridges, a scale along the bottom edge, and a bronze registration hole. The most minimal and graphic."
      - key: g
        name: "G · Firm block"
        note: "A drawing sheet's firm block: heavy outer border, medium divider, fine rule. In the nav it becomes a horizontal lockup — ZT cell, then Zachery Taylor over Civil Designer · EI. The square ZT cell is the favicon."
  - title: "Round 1"
    label: "B-001"
    options:
      - key: a
        name: "A · Title block"
        note: "Z and T share one top stroke, set inside a blueprint sheet frame with a title-block strip — the drawing-set motif used across the site."
      - key: b
        name: "B · Serif ligature"
        note: "Instrument Serif Z overlapped by an italic blueprint-blue T, on paper with a bronze rule. The most literary — leans toward the book."
      - key: c
        name: "C · Benchmark"
        note: "A survey benchmark disk: graduated ring, section-marker circle split by a datum line, ZT above and a benchmark triangle below."
---
{%- import "macros.njk" as ui with context -%}
<style>
  .mono-grid { display: grid; gap: 28px; }
  .mono { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr 1fr; border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; background: rgb(var(--surface) / .8); }
  .mono > div { padding: 26px; }
  .mono .info h2 { font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .mono .info p { color: var(--muted); font-size: .95rem; }
  .mono .current { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 10px; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--action); color: #fff; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .swatch { display: grid; gap: 18px; align-content: start; }
  .swatch.light { background: #f3f0e8; color: #0f1419; }
  .swatch.dark { background: #0f1419; color: #f3f0e8; }
  .swatch .k { font-size: .66rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; opacity: .75; }
  .big svg { width: 168px; height: 168px; }
  .row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; }
  .tab { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 7px 12px; border-radius: 9px 9px 0 0; background: #fff; color: #333; font-size: .78rem; box-shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.08); }
  .dark .tab { background: #262c33; color: #ddd; }
  .tab svg { width: 16px; height: 16px; }
  .fav32 svg { width: 32px; height: 32px; }
  .navmock { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; font-weight: 700; font-size: .95rem; }
  .navmock svg { width: 40px; height: 40px; }
  .navmock.lockupmock svg { width: auto; height: 40px; }
  .big-lockup svg { width: 100%; max-width: 340px; height: auto; }
  .round-title { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 14px; margin: 8px 0 -6px; }
  .round-title h2 { font-size: 1.7rem; }
  .navmock small { display: block; font-size: .62rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; opacity: .7; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .mono { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
<header class="page-header">
  <div class="wrap">
    {{ ui.sectionLabel("B-001", "For review") }}
    <h1>Monogram <em>options.</em></h1>
    <p class="lead">Seven directions for the ZT mark — four new ones in round 2, plus the original three — each shown as a browser-tab favicon (16 and 32&nbsp;px), at navigation size (40&nbsp;px), and large, on paper and on ink. Option {{ site.monogram | upper }} is live in the nav, footer, and favicons right now. To switch, change <code>monogram: "{{ site.monogram }}"</code> in <code>site.config.js</code> to any letter <code>"a"</code>–<code>"g"</code>.</p>
  </div>
</header>
<section class="band" aria-label="Options">
  <div class="wrap mono-grid">
    {%- for r in rounds %}
    <div class="round-title">{{ ui.sectionLabel(r.label, r.title) }}</div>
    {%- for o in r.options %}
    {%- set lk = o.key | lockup %}
    <article class="mono" aria-labelledby="opt-{{ o.key }}">
      <div class="info">
        {%- if o.key == site.monogram %}<span class="current">IN USE</span>{% endif %}
        <h2 id="opt-{{ o.key }}">{{ o.name }}</h2>
        <p>{{ o.note }}</p>
        <p style="margin-top:14px"><a href="/assets/brand/monogram-{{ o.key }}.svg">Download SVG</a>{% if lk %} · <a href="/assets/brand/lockup-{{ o.key }}.svg">Lockup SVG</a>{% endif %}</p>
      </div>
      {%- for tone in ["light", "dark"] %}
      <div class="swatch {{ tone }}">
        <span class="k">{{ "On paper" if tone == "light" else "On ink" }}</span>
        <div class="row"><span class="tab">{{ o.key | monogram | safe }} Zachery Taylor</span><span class="fav32">{{ o.key | monogram | safe }}</span></div>
        {%- if lk %}
        <span class="navmock lockupmock">{{ lk | safe }}</span>
        {%- else %}
        <span class="navmock">{{ o.key | monogram | safe }}<span>Zachery Taylor<small>Civil Designer · EI</small></span></span>
        {%- endif %}
        <div class="big">{{ o.key | monogram | safe }}</div>
        {%- if lk %}<div class="big-lockup">{{ lk | safe }}</div>{% endif %}
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </article>
    {%- endfor %}
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
